# {{ project_name }} — generated by Ansible-Z

Infrastructure: **{{ _meta.name }}** (v{{ _meta.version }}, PCI: {{ _meta.pci }}) · environment: **{{ env }}**

A VPN-only microservices platform: corporate/VPN access → public **ALB** →
**Kong** API gateway (ECS Fargate) → private **ECS** microservices → **RDS MySQL**
(Multi-AZ), with a **bastion** for SSH. Five least-privilege security groups
chain the tiers together.

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Region | `{{ aws_region }}` |
| VPC CIDR | `{{ vpc_cidr }}` |
| Service image | `{{ service_image }}` |
| Kong image | `{{ kong_image | default('kong:3.6') }}` |
| VPN / bastion access | `{{ office_ip | default('set office_ip') }}` |

## Traffic path
`VPN → ALB (80/443) → Kong SG → Kong (8000) → ECS SG → microservices (8080) → RDS SG → MySQL (3306)`.
Nothing is reachable from the internet except the ALB; the bastion is the only SSH entry point.

## Run
```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install ansible boto3 botocore
ansible-galaxy collection install -r collections/requirements.yml
aws configure                                   # credentials for {{ aws_region }}

ansible-playbook preflight.yml                  # checks creds + variables
ansible-playbook site.yml --check               # dry run
ansible-playbook site.yml                        # provision
```

> Put `db_password` in **ansible-vault**. Attach a real ACM certificate to the ALB
> for HTTPS:443, and complete the VPN (customer gateway + connection) to the VPN gateway.
